{"step_index":762,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-20T18:11:53Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Detailed root cause analysis and resolution of boot screen stall: removed blocking bootloader conditions, wrapped app in Root ErrorBoundary, sanitized localStorage parsing with defensive array fallbacks, and re-deployed cleanly to Surge.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"# Walkthrough: Root Cause Correction for Startup Screen & Live Re-Deployment\\n\\nThe **SnapDialer** app at [`C:\\\\Users\\\\brorm\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\snap-dialer`](file:///C:/Users/brorm/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/snap-dialer) has been thoroughly audited and patched:\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Deep Root Cause Analysis:\\n1. **Bootloader Blocking Issue:**\\n   - `App.tsx` had a state gate `if (!dbReady)` rendering a dark blue loading screen `#0F172A` that could stall if previous list-seeding logic or asynchronous storage parsing encountered legacy browser state.\\n2. **Defensive Storage Parsing:**\\n   - `WebDatabase` now wraps all `localStorage` reads in defensive checks ensuring `lists`, `leads`, `call_logs`, and `settings` always evaluate to clean, initialized arrays even if historical cache contains legacy schemas.\\n3. **App ErrorBoundary Added:**\\n   - Wrapped the entire application tree in a top-level `ErrorBoundary` that renders explicit diagnostic details instead of a silent blank screen if any unhandled error ever occurs.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Live Surge Deployment:\\n- Deployed live to: **`https://valuteachers-dialer.surge.sh`**\\n\"","Description":"\"Walkthrough documenting startup fix and Surge deployment\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\brorm\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\9c9b5ef4-82a1-483f-9e9e-cb421c9396b3\\\\walkthrough.md\"","toolAction":"\"Updating walkthrough for startup screen fix\"","toolSummary":"\"Update walkthrough.md with root cause fixes\""}}]}
